# Coding Standards

## Hard Constraints (NEVER violate)

- Type error suppression (`as any`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`) -- NEVER
- Empty catch blocks `catch(e) {}` -- ALWAYS handle errors
- Commit without explicit user request -- NEVER
- Speculate about unread code -- NEVER read it first
- Deleting failing tests to make them pass -- NEVER

## Code Quality

- Match existing codebase patterns before introducing new ones
- Add comments only for non-obvious intent, trade-offs, or constraints
- Avoid AI-generated comment patterns: "// Import the module", "// Define the function", "// Return the result"
- No catch-all files (utils.ts, helpers.ts, service.ts)
- Fix root causes, not symptoms

## File Organization

- index.ts is entry point ONLY -- never dump business logic there
- 200 LOC soft limit per file (prompt templates exempt)
- kebab-case for all files and directories
- Relative imports within module, barrel imports across modules

## Error Handling

- Every catch block must handle the error meaningfully
- Log errors with context (what operation failed, with what inputs)
- Fail fast on unrecoverable errors
- Use typed errors where the language supports it
